122 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Must have\nAs a user\054 when I press and hold the START button for one second\054 I expect the interface to turn on\056\nAs a user\054 when I press and hold START again while the machine is on\054 I expect the display to turn off\056\nAs a user\054 when I tap or drag the Stitch Pattern slider\054 I expect the needle bar moves along with it\054 and the preview\054 the status label \050STITCHING \057 HEMMING \057 BUTTON\051 and the middle bar to update\054 so that I can confirm which stitch the machine will sew before I start\056\nAs a user\054 when I touch the Stitch Pattern slider while the machine is off\054 I expect nothing to change\054 so that I don\031t change settings by accident while the machine is off\056\nAs a user\054 when I move the Speed slider\054 I expect the needle bar moves along with it\056\nAs a user\054 when I pinch or spread two fingers on the stitch preview\054 I expect the stitch in the preview and in the middle bar to get smaller or bigger\054 so that I can adjust stitch size to fit my fabric\056\n\nNice to have\nAs a user\054 when I move the Speed slider\054 I expect the middle bar to update\054 so that I can confirm which speed the machine will sew before I start\056\n\nDropped\n Dropped\072 a single tap is too easy to trigger by accident on a handheld tool with a needle\054 so a long press is safer\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 121 0 R
     /Pg 118 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
